'' __FB_64BIT__ came from an '#ifdef' at tiko-lang's OWN compile time, so it was true even
'' for '-target linux-x86_64'. Getting it wrong does not fail -- it silently selects
'' the other half of every header, and the corpus branches on it 214 times.
''
'' WHAT THIS PROVES. win32 is the target on which __FB_64BIT__ is ABSENT, so
'' the target-derived macro is checked directly there; linux-x86_64 from a
'' Windows host remains the cross-platform witness.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --pp-only -target linux-x86_64 tests/driver/src/predefines.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: HAS64
'' EXPECT-OUT: LIN
'' EXPECT-NOT: WIN
'' STEP: -target win32 --pp-only tests/driver/src/predefines.bas
'' STEP-OUT: NO64
'' STEP-OUT: WIN
